{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "mixed-onroad fixture",
    "description": "The `mixed-onroad` fixture: 250 rows of MOVESOutput -- running-exhaust Total Energy Consumption for passenger cars on urban restricted-access roads in Washtenaw County, August, 9am, 2020 -- computed from the snapshot's own INPUT tables. Ports docs/mixed-onroad.md end to end: the activity chain S1-S9, the cohort structure and the fuel-usage rebase S10-S12, the drive-cycle operating-mode weights and the base rate S13-S14, the calculator's adjustments S15 and the output row S16-S18.\n\nWHAT IS COMPUTED AND WHAT IS DECLARED.\n\nCOMPUTED, from the input tables and nothing else: every number. In particular `dc_W[dayType, opModeID]`, the speed-bin-weighted drive-cycle operating-mode distribution -- 46 numbers that \u00a78.1 recorded as the ONE relation this port could not compute, because MOVES 5 computes it inside the worker and drops it. It is computed here from `driveschedulesecond`'s 63,602 second-by-second speeds, and the four neighbouring-second reads it needs are `driveschedulesecond` joined to ITSELF, which finding F11 refused until EarthSciAST 107a15152. NO REFERENCE TABLE IS AN INPUT. `baserate_1_2020`, `sourcebindistributionfuelusage_1_26161_2020`, `sho` and `MOVESOutput` are all generator or expected output, and none of them is a `data_sources` entry here -- nothing flows from them into a number. Values out of the first and third DO appear, as `expected` in the inline tests below, which is the opposite direction and the whole point of a fixture: `cohDay_meanBaseRate` is checked against what `baserate_1_2020` stores and `act_sho` against what `sho` stores, and if either check is deleted the arithmetic is unchanged.\n\nCOMPUTED, and worth saying because a reader would assume otherwise: the SHAPES. The activity relation's 82 rows are `n_agecategory x n_runspecday` and the cohort candidate grid's 164 are `n_agecategory x n_runspecsourcefueltype`, both metaparameter expressions over extents the runtime discovers from the files.\n\nDECLARED: one number, `n_outputCohort` = 125, the length of the output relation's cohort block. WHICH 125 of the 164 candidates survive is a result of the chain -- \u00a72.2's `stmyFraction > 0` rule -- and materialising them as an index set is finding F5's value invention, which validates and materialises EMPTY. So the count is declared, as fixtures/nr-logging-county.esm and fixtures/process-evap-leaks.esm declare theirs, and three things keep it honest: the surviving cohorts are reached by a RANK (docs/esm-conventions.md \u00a722) rather than by a transcribed block map, so no key column is written down; `cohortSurvivorCount` computes 125 from the chain and a test pins the two together; and the comparator's exact key set fails on any row whose rank found no cohort.\n\nTHE PACKED IDENTIFIER IS NEVER BUILT, ONLY UNPACKED. `emissionrate`'s 69,200 rows carry `sourceBinID` = 1e18 + fuel x 1e16 + engTech x 1e14 + regClass x 1e12 + shortModYrGroup x 1e10, about 1.01e18 and past 2^53. `lib/onroad_activity.esm`'s `source_bin_slot` reads the four components out; nothing here composes one, and no element type is declared for the same reason (\u00a72.2, finding F18).\n\nTWO CLAMPS EVALUATE TO ZERO HERE AND BOTH ARE COMPUTED, not assumed. The A/C activity term is -0.0189 at 66.9 degF and clamps to 0; the EV temperature term is -0.00419 and clamps to 0. Both are within 0.3 degF of turning on -- the A/C one is worth 14.6% of the MY1980 gasoline rate -- so this document computes both from `monthgrouphour`, `zonemonthhour` and `temperatureadjustment` rather than writing the zero down. What the FIXTURE cannot check is what those zeros multiply: `cohDay_meanBaseRateACAdj` is modelled because \u00a72.3(a) is part of S13 and a document without it is incomplete, but it reaches the answer through an exactly-zero factor and docs/esm-conventions.md \u00a723 says a stage in that position is not to be checked THROUGH THE OUTPUT -- but `baserate_1_2020` carries it in its own column, so it is asserted directly instead, and it agrees to 3.6e-07. What genuinely cannot be checked at this fixture is the NON-ZERO arm of the A/C factor, which needs a different hour; components/onroad_energy_output.esm moves the heat index and asserts both arms of both clamps.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "moves",
      "onroad",
      "energy",
      "fixture",
      "mixed-onroad"
    ]
  },
