      "type": "integer",
      "default": 125,
      "description": "THE ONE DECLARED NUMBER IN THIS DOCUMENT: how many (modelYearID, fuelTypeID) cohorts reach MOVESOutput. 125 of the 164 candidates, ragged by fuel -- 41 gasoline model years, 40 diesel, 23 E85 and 21 electricity, because those are the years before E85 and electric drive existed and the year diesel passenger cars stopped. WHICH ones survive is a result of \u00a72.2's `stmyFraction > 0` rule and is never written down: `coh_rank` numbers the survivors 1..125 by an inclusive prefix count over the candidate grid and the output row joins to that rank (docs/esm-conventions.md \u00a722), so both key columns come from the chain. `cohortSurvivorCount` recomputes 125 from the chain and a test pins the two together, so a rule that admitted 124 or 126 fails here before the comparator sees a row."
    }
