        "evTemperatureReferenceDegF": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 72.0,
          "description": "adjust.rs:108. The EV branch's reference temperature is 72 degF where the standard quadratic's is 75; that is not a typo in either place."
        },
        "evTemperatureSourceTypeCeiling": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 40.0,
          "description": "adjust.rs:114. The heat-index suppression applies to source types below 40, i.e. light duty. Source type 21 qualifies, so the suppression is LIVE here and returns 1 only because 66.9 < 67."
        },
        "evTemperatureSuppressionHeatIndex": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 67.0,
          "description": "adjust.rs:114. The fixture's 66.900001525879 is one tenth of a degree below this, so the suppression does NOT fire and the EV factor is 1 by its own `adj < 0` clamp instead -- two different reasons for the same 1, and \u00a77.2 shows they diverge 0.3 degF away."
        },
        "idleCeilingMph": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "drivecycle.rs:230. A second below 1 mph is Idling; at national scale a second at exactly 0 mph is Idling too rather than the project-scale mode 501, so the two arms collapse to this one predicate."
        },
