        "cohMode_rate": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "cohort_rows",
            "operating_mode_rows"
          ],
          "description": "J22: emissionrate keyed on the four unpacked bin COMPONENTS plus the pollutant-process and the operating mode, as ONE clause -- a single composite key. THE ORIGINAL REASON IS GONE AND THE FUSION STAYS ANYWAY, which is worth stating so a reader does not retire it a second time. It was written this way because document order picked the driving clause and six separate clauses cost 158,030,400 leaves against this composite's 3,772 (finding F17). F17 is fixed: the conjunctive gate reaches the same 3,772 from the six-clause spelling, and the six-clause form emits a BYTE-IDENTICAL relation, so nothing here depends on the fusion for correctness or for avoiding a blow-up. But equal leaves are not equal cost -- six clauses build six equijoins where one composite builds one -- and measured on this fixture `esm simulate` is 2.8 s fused against 5.1 s unfused, three runs each, a consistent 1.85x. So this is now a MEASURED authoring choice rather than a workaround: docs/esm-conventions.md \u00a725 is retired as a rule and this is not an instance of it."
        },
