          "_comment": "J22: ONE clause carrying six key pairs, and THIS IS A COST DECISION, not a reading order (docs/esm-conventions.md \u00a725). Splitting it into six one-pair clauses gives a byte-identical answer and takes 43x as long -- measured on this document, 298.36 s and 287.08 s against 6.61 / 6.62 / 6.98 s. Six pairs in one clause is ONE composite gate admitting 3,772 leaves over the 164 x 60 output cells; six clauses is a gate whose selectivity is that of whichever single pair resolves first, which for the order these pairs are written in is `fuelTypeID` at 1.58e8 leaves. docs/mixed-onroad.md \u00a710.3 has the table for all six.",
