        },
        {
          "id": "the_collapsed_base_rate_reproduces_the_references_own_intermediate",
          "description": "`cohDay_meanBaseRate` IS `baserate_1_2020.meanBaseRate` -- the reference's own S14 intermediate, and the relation docs/mixed-onroad.md \u00a78.1 recorded as the one this port could not compute. Asserted here against the values that table stores, which is the most direct check of W available: \u00a77.3 shows the base rate factorises exactly around W, so a wrong W is a wrong number in every one of these cells and nothing else in the chain can absorb it. Four cohorts over both day types, chosen to span four orders of magnitude and all four fuel types' behaviour: MY1980 gasoline (the largest rate), MY2020 gasoline, MY2020 electricity (the youngest EV age group) and MY2000 electricity (the oldest, and the smallest rate in the fixture).\n\n`cohDay_meanBaseRateACAdj` is the INCREMENTAL A/C load of sbweighted.rs:459, and it is asserted for a reason the fixture's own description hedges about: it reaches emissionQuant multiplied by an A/C factor this document computes to be exactly 0, so the OUTPUT cannot see it -- but `baserate_1_2020` carries it in its own column, so it can be checked here anyway. What remains uncheckable at this fixture is the non-zero arm of the A/C FACTOR, which needs a different hour; components/onroad_energy_output.esm moves the heat index and asserts both arms.\n\nThe tolerance is the reference's six-significant-figure column storage.\n\nFALSIFIED, and the measurement is why this test exists at all. A SUM-PRESERVING perturbation of the classification -- `dss_vsp` x 1.001, so a handful of seconds cross a VSP boundary into a neighbouring mode -- leaves `dc_WTotal` at 1.0000004 and `dc_WModeCount` at 23, i.e. INVISIBLE to both of W's structural tests, and fails nine of these thirteen assertions and all four worked examples. The structural tests check that W is a distribution; only a value does.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "tolerance": {
            "rel": 2e-05
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "cohDay_meanBaseRate",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 387171.0,
              "coords": {
                "cohort_rows": 41,
                "runspecday_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "cohDay_meanBaseRate",
