        {
          "id": "the_temperature_lookup_reaches_the_regClassID_zero_wildcard",
          "description": "adjust.rs:495-520 looks a temperatureadjustment row up by the exact regClassID and THEN by the regClassID 0 wildcard. This document used to implement only the first step, and the only row in the table is the wildcard -- so its EV temperature terms came out 0, its raw adjustment 0 instead of -0.00419, and the `adj < 0` clamp returned the right factor of 1 FOR THE WRONG REASON. Invisible here and a 1.56 % error at 59.5 degF, which is where fixtures/process-brakewear.esm found it. The precedence is now lib/adjustments.esm's `exact_else_wildcard` and both fixtures instantiate it.\\n\\nThe assertions below are what would go red if the wildcard step were removed again: the exact-class lookup finds nothing, the resolved terms are the wildcard row's, and the raw adjustment is NEGATIVE -- the thing the clamp then does its job on. Cohort 144 is (MY 2000, electricity), docs/mixed-onroad.md 6.3's worked example C.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "tolerance": {
            "rel": 2e-06
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "coh_hasTempAdjustExact",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "cohort_rows": 144
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "coh_tempAdjustTermA",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.00225,
              "coords": {
                "cohort_rows": 144
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "coh_tempAdjustTermB",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.00028,
              "coords": {
                "cohort_rows": 144
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "coh_evTemperatureAdjustRaw",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": -0.0041922,
              "coords": {
                "cohort_rows": 144
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "coh_evTemperatureFactor",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "cohort_rows": 144
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "coh_tempAdjustTermA",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "cohort_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "coh_evTemperatureFactor",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1.0,
              "coords": {
                "cohort_rows": 1
              }
            }
          ]
        }
